## Solution

**Setup.** Place $B=(0,0)$, $C=(14,0)$. From $AB=13$, $AC=15$:
$$a^2+h^2=169,\quad (a-14)^2+h^2=225 \;\Rightarrow\; a=5,\; h=12.$$
So $A=(5,12)$, $H=(5,0)$. Area $=84$, $s=21$, $r=4$. Tangent point $D$: $BD=s-CA=6$, so $D=(6,0)$. Incenter $I=\tfrac{14A+15B+13C}{42}=(6,4)$.

**Circumcircle.** Center on $x=7$: $O=(7,k)$, and $49+k^2=4+(12-k)^2 \Rightarrow k=\tfrac{33}{8}$. So $O=(7,\tfrac{33}{8})$, $R^2=\tfrac{4225}{64}$.

**Point $E$** (second intersection of $AI$ with $(O)$). Line $AI$: $(5+t,12-8t)$. Substituting:
$$(t-2)^2+\Big(\tfrac{63}{8}-8t\Big)^2=\tfrac{4225}{64}\;\Rightarrow\;65t^2-130t=0.$$
$t=0$ ($A$) or $t=2$: $\;E=(7,-4)$.

**Point $F$** (second intersection of $ED$ with $(O)$). Line $ED$: $(7-s,-4+4s)$. Substituting:
$$s^2+\Big(\tfrac{-65}{8}+4s\Big)^2=\tfrac{4225}{64}\;\Rightarrow\;17s^2-65s=0.$$
$s=\tfrac{65}{17}$: $\;F=\big(\tfrac{54}{17},\tfrac{192}{17}\big)$.

**Point $L$** (second intersection of $EH$ with $(O)$). Line $EH$: $(7-u,-4+2u)$. Substituting:
$$u^2+\Big(\tfrac{-65}{8}+2u\Big)^2=\tfrac{4225}{64}\;\Rightarrow\;5u^2-\tfrac{65}{2}u=0.$$
$u=\tfrac{13}{2}$: $\;L=\big(\tfrac{1}{2},9\big)$.

**Tangent at $F$.** Radius slope: $\dfrac{192/17-33/8}{54/17-7}=\dfrac{975/136}{-65/17}=-\dfrac{15}{8}$, so tangent slope $=\dfrac{8}{15}$:
$$y-\tfrac{192}{17}=\tfrac{8}{15}\Big(x-\tfrac{54}{17}\Big).\tag{1}$$

**Line $AL$.** Slope $=\dfrac{9-12}{1/2-5}=\dfrac{2}{3}$, so
$$y=\frac{26+2x}{3}.\tag{2}$$

**Intersection $T$.** Substituting (2) into (1):
$$\frac{26+2x}{3}-\frac{192}{17}=\frac{8}{15}\Big(x-\frac{54}{17}\Big).$$
$$\frac{34x-134}{51}=\frac{8(17x-54)}{255}\;\Rightarrow\;5(34x-134)=8(17x-54)$$
$$170x-670=136x-432\;\Rightarrow\;34x=238\;\Rightarrow\;x=7.$$
Then $y=\tfrac{26+14}{3}=\tfrac{40}{3}$, so $T=\big(7,\tfrac{40}{3}\big)$.

**Verification of $TB=TC$.** Since $T_x=7$ is the midpoint of $BC$ (which spans $0$ to $14$), $T$ lies on the perpendicular bisector of $BC$, hence $TB=TC$ automatically. ✓

**Compute $x^2$.**
$$x^2=TB^2=7^2+\Big(\frac{40}{3}\Big)^2=49+\frac{1600}{9}=\frac{441+1600}{9}=\frac{2041}{9}.$$

$$\boxed{x^2=\dfrac{2041}{9}}$$

